  "label": "the overallintent",
  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image features a smiling woman of color holding a small American flag, with overlaid text that reads: \"i say woman of color because i want to be inclusive of all but white women.\" This text is a deliberately exclusionary and racist statement, using the term \"woman of color\" to exclude white women from a supposed \"inclusive\" group. The meme's intent is to mock and demean the concept of inclusivity by framing it as a form of exclusionary racism, targeting white women specifically. It weaponizes the term \"woman of color\" to imply that white women are not included in the category, which is a harmful and hateful trope rooted in racial hierarchy. The visual of a Black woman (who is often associated with the term \"woman of color\") is juxtaposed with the text to create a false equivalence and to imply that her identity is being used to exclude others. This is a hateful meme that promotes racial division and exclusion, and it is designed to provoke a reaction by highlighting the perceived hypocrisy or exclusionary nature of the term \"woman of color\" when applied to exclude white women. The meme is not merely a joke but a direct attack on the inclusivity of the term, and it is intended to be offensive and divisive. The overall intent is to spread a hateful message that reinforces racial hierarchies and exclusionary practices.",
